            <div xml:id="d646">

                <pb facs="0940" n="834" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg834"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.6131/559: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grummon</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-08-03T19:00:00-04:00">August 3, 1939—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>113. Your 417, July 31, 10 p.m. Was it your impression that Mikoyan meant that the Soviet Government was
                    not interested in obtaining tariff reductions in connection with a possible
                    trade agreement or did he merely intend to inform you that the Soviet Government
                    would not pursue the matter in connection with this commercial agreement? Please
                    do not raise the question with Soviet officials.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
